# D10(a) NEGATIVE (decisions.md, ratified 2026-07-06): the decl-sigil form of
# a local `&`-bind (`Vector[int] &r = a`) is a PARSE error. Pre-D10 the
# parser silently DISCARDED the sigil (only `mutable` set the flag), so the
# binding was a plain value copy that READ as a reference declaration —
# mutations through `r` never reached `a`.
# Expected: parse error "local `&`-bindings are not supported".
void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3]
    Vector[int] &r = a
    r.push(9)
    print(a.len())
